<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tang of Shang</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cheng Tang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tang of Shang, also called Cheng Tang, was the founder of the Shang dynasty according to Chinese tradition. Histories such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sima-qian">Sima Qian</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/records-of-the-grand-historian">Shiji</a> relate that he overthrew Jie, the tyrannical last king of the Xia, at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mingtiao">Battle of Mingtiao</a>, with the help of his minister Yi Yin. Oracle-bone inscriptions honour him as Da Yi, an important founding ancestor of the Shang kings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tang-of-shang.jpg" alt="Tang of Shang" width="320" height="704" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ma Lin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Tang_of_Shang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
